    "_note": "Re-pinned 2026-08-11 WITH export_curtailment_active honoured. test_scenarios previously rebuilt the optimizer call by hand and dropped export_curtailment_active, initial_cost_basis and home_settings, so this fixture -- which exists to pin #510's charge-early tie-break UNDER the export-curtailment price floor -- was asserted with curtailment OFF, the one condition it was captured for. The suite now passes _scenario_inputs through whole, as golden_capture.py already did. Cost moves -2.74447 -> -2.765873 (0.0214 SEK cheaper; savings 10.62582 -> 10.647224): the correct-inputs solve was always the better one, nothing regressed. Post-fix (charge-early tie-break under the #269 curtailment floor) pin. These economics do NOT discriminate pre/post fix at the harness's 1-decimal tolerance -- the defect is an exact reward tie, so planned cost barely moves. The discriminating pin is test_curtailment_charge_early_tiebreak.py, which asserts the SOE trajectory absorbs below-floor surplus immediately (full by period 6, not period 9). Re-pinned after #497 (PR #511) removed the phantom sub-resolution export revenue, and again at #512's finer DP grid. Note this is the raw-DP figure test_scenarios measures (build_scenario_inputs does not pass export_curtailment_active); under helpers._scenario_inputs, which does pass it, #507's curtailed-period reporting adjustment moves the planned cost to -2.76587, leaving the +0.0214 execution gap pinned in test_plan_faithfulness.KNOWN_PLAN_EXECUTION_GAP_SEK (#502). Re-pinned again 2026-08-16 for #606, which added tie_policy row 5 (canonical order among value-indistinguishable candidates, within the winner's own action class). Cost moves -2.765873 -> -2.764334: +0.00154 SEK worse, the largest regression the row causes anywhere in the corpus and inside the #450 0.05 SEK budget. It is interpolation residual, not a forfeited preference: row 5 only reorders candidates whose DP values are within 1e-12, and an exact tie in interpolated value is not an exact tie in realized cost. Corpus-wide the row is net favourable (-0.03746 SEK over 4 fixtures; synthetic_clear_sky_ac_clipping alone improves 0.039). #510's charge-early tie-break is untouched -- row 5 stands down whenever an earlier row moved the pick, and never changes the action's class -- and test_curtailment_charge_early_tiebreak.py still pins the SOE trajectory."
